  "title": "India's Credit Rating Agencies Push for Wider Lenses on Infrastructure",
  "summary": "Gautam Adani urges India's rating agencies to develop broader analytical frameworks for infrastructure projects, arguing that conventional models may underestimate the economic and strategic value of large integrated platforms. Adani emphasizes the need for wider lenses to assess infrastructure that extends beyond cash flows, aligning with India's broader goals of building a more developed economy.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Gautam Adani urged India's credit-rating agencies to develop new credit frameworks for infrastructure projects.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Adani emphasized that conventional models may understate the value of large integrated platforms creating new markets and industrial ecosystems.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
